\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The potential term}
\date{2026-11-03}


\p{The [multiplication operator](fdip-00AI) #{M_V} is the potential term
of a lattice Schrödinger operator, added to a difference operator. The
assignment #{f\mapsto M_f} is how a field acts on its own module, and
#{M_f M_g=M_g M_f}. A shift need not commute with #{M_f}. That product
is the operator product of \ref{fdip-0011}, and \ref{fdip-00AP}
computes the failure on a cycle.}
